  "response": "### Retrospective Analysis: Score History & Key Pattern\n\nOver the last seven editions, **THE VISSION** scored perfectly ($25/25$) in five consecutive runs (Sept 2 to Sept 6), but dropped points on August 28 ($17/25$) and September 1 ($21/25$). \n\nThe single pattern costing the paper the most points is **Balance** (specifically **empty beats across consecutive editions**):\n- **August 28:** Scored **2 on Balance** (a revise-level failure) because three beats were empty, with India specifically running zero stories for two straight editions.\n- **September 1:** Scored **4 on Balance** due to the `infrastructure` beat running empty.\n\n---\n\n### Machine Check Implementation\n\nI implemented a permanent machine check in `tools/validate.mjs` that looks back at the chronologically preceding edition and ensures no beat runs empty ($0$ stories) for two consecutive editions. \n\nThis check is fully gated to prevent breaking historical editions:\n- **Prior to 2026-09-07:** Triggers a **warning** (`warn`) so the archive continues to pass validation on normal runs.\n- **On or after 2026-09-07:** Triggers a **hard error** (`err`) which blocks the publish gate in `--strict` mode.\n\n#### Code Diff (`git diff tools/validate.mjs`):\n```diff\ndiff --git a/tools/validate.mjs b/tools/validate.mjs\nindex bf689f0..afdaf07 100644\n--- a/tools/validate.mjs\n+++ b/tools/validate.mjs\n@@ -299,6 +299,26 @@ function jaccard(a, b) {\n   return shared / (a.size + b.size - shared);\n }\n \n+/**\n+ * Finds and loads the edition immediately preceding the currentDate.\n+ */\n+function getPreviousEdition(currentDate) {\n+  try {\n+    const files = readdirSync(GENERATED)\n+      .filter((f) => /^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\.json$/.test(f))\n+      .sort();\n+    for (let i = files.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n+      const date = files[i].slice(0, 10);\n+      if (date < currentDate) {\n+        return readJSON(join(GENERATED, files[i]));\n+      }\n+    }\n+  } catch {\n+    return null;\n+  }\n+  return null;\n+}\n+\n function checkEdition(file) {\n   const errors = [];\n   const warnings = [];\n@@ -572,6 +592,7 @@ function checkEdition(file) {\n   checkEvalBinding(doc, err, warn);\n \n   // --- beat coverage --------------------------------------------------------\n+  const prevDoc = getPreviousEdition(doc.edition.date);\n   for (const beat of beats) {\n     const count = stories.filter((s) => s.beat === beat.id).length;\n     if (count < beat.minQuota) {\n@@ -579,6 +600,19 @@ function checkEdition(file) {\n     } else if (count < beat.quota) {\n       advise(`beat \"${beat.id}\" has ${count} stories, target is ${beat.quota}`);\n     }\n+\n+    if (count === 0 && prevDoc) {\n+      const prevStories = prevDoc.stories || [];\n+      const prevCount = prevStories.filter((s) => s.beat === beat.id).length;\n+      if (prevCount === 0) {\n+        const msg = `beat \"${beat.id}\" has 0 stories for two consecutive editions (${prevDoc.edition.date} and ${doc.edition.date})`;\n+        if (gated) {\n+          err(msg);\n+        } else {\n+          warn(msg);\n+        }\n+      }\n+    }\n   }\n \n   return { file, errors, warnings, advisories };\n```\n\n---\n\n### Pull Request Draft\n\nDue to security policies restricting git checkout and commit execution, here is the exact draft of the pull request to be raised:\n\n*   **Branch Name:** `retro/empty-beat-validation`\n*   **Commit Message:** `validate: check for empty beats across consecutive editions`\n*   **PR Title:** `Retrospective: consecutive empty beats harming Balance score`\n\n#### PR Body:\n```markdown\n### Evidence from Score History\nIn the last seven runs, Balance has been the single costliest scoring dimension:\n- **2026-08-28:** Balance scored a revise-level 2 because three beats (infrastructure, society, india) ran empty. India ran zero stories for two straight editions.\n- **2026-09-01:** Balance scored 4 due to an empty infrastructure beat.\n\n### Specific Fix\nAdded `getPreviousEdition()` and a machine check inside `tools/validate.mjs` to block publishing if a beat has 0 stories for two consecutive editions.\n- Older historical editions (before 2026-09-07) emit a warning so existing archive builds stay green.\n- Future editions (from 2026-09-07 forward) fail the strict publish gate on consecutive empty beats.\n\n### What it would have caught\nThis machine check would have flagged the empty India beat on August 28 and blocked publication until a relevant India-beat story was surfaced, preventing the score drop to 17/25.\n```",
